IMPORT prelude

-- Casino Control Act 2006 (Singapore) -- the patron's side: the entry levy (s 116), credit (s 108), minors (ss 132 to 134), and
-- family exclusion orders (s 162).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CCA2006.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 29 of 2024 (parts in force 30 October 2024 and 21 September 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 13 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a patron and the patron's family
-- meet. Not encoded: licensing of casinos, operators, special employees and international market agents, the Authority, games and
-- equipment, junkets, AML duties, disciplinary action, self- and third-party exclusion procedure, visit limits, and taxes.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Casino Control Act 2006 -- patrons`

§§ `116 -- the entry levy`

-- s 116(1): a casino operator must not let a CITIZEN or PERMANENT RESIDENT enter or remain unless they have paid (a) $150 for every
-- consecutive 24 hours, or (b) $3,000 for an annual membership. (3): no refund, remission or reimbursement. (5), (6): employees and
-- officers on duty are exempt but must not gamble. (7): a citizen or PR who enters without paying -- a fine up to $1,500, and the
-- $150 levy. Foreigners pay nothing.
GIVEN `is citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `periods of 24 hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the entry levy payable` MEANS
    IF `is citizen or PR` THEN `periods of 24 hours` TIMES 150 ELSE 0

GIVEN `is citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `days intended this year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annual membership is cheaper` IF
    `is citizen or PR` AND `days intended this year` TIMES 150 GREATER THAN 3000

§§ `108 -- credit`

-- s 108(1): lending money, or providing chips on credit (including by credit card), is prohibited, except (7) a casino operator may
-- give credit to (a) a person who is neither a citizen nor a PR, (b) a PREMIUM PLAYER, or (c) a licensed international market agent.
-- s 2: a premium player keeps a deposit account with a credit balance of at least $100,000.
--
-- The exception for premium players does not depend on nationality: a citizen with $100,000 on deposit can be given credit.
GIVEN `is citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `deposit balance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the casino may give the patron credit` IF
    (NOT `is citizen or PR`) OR `deposit balance` AT LEAST 100000

§§ `132 to 134 -- minors`

-- s 132: "minor" means a person below 21; a minor must not enter, remain or gamble -- a fine up to $1,500 (the minor's offence).
-- s 133(1): the operator must not permit a minor to enter. (5): it is a DEFENCE that the minor was 16 OR OVER and acceptable proof of
-- age was produced. (A forged ID shown by a 15-year-old is no defence for the operator.)
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a minor for the Act` IF
    `age` LESS THAN 21

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `proof of age produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator has a defence for admitting the minor` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 16 AND `proof of age produced`

§§ `162 -- family exclusion orders`

-- s 162(1): a Committee may make a family exclusion order if there is a reasonable apprehension the respondent may cause serious harm
-- to family members by gambling, the order is appropriate, the respondent had the opportunity to object, and it is in the best
-- interests of the respondent and family. (2): serious harm means gambling irresponsibly without regard to the family's needs "repeatedly
-- over a period of NOT LESS THAN 3 MONTHS or in a particularly irresponsible manner over a lesser period". (3): apprehension needs past
-- harm on that test plus reason to believe it will continue. (4): events outside Singapore count.
DECLARE Respondent HAS
    `gambled irresponsibly ignoring the family's needs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of repeated irresponsible gambling` IS A NUMBER
    `particularly irresponsible over a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to continue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given the chance to object` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the best interests of all` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the respondent` IS A Respondent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `serious harm has been caused` IF
        `the respondent`'s `gambled irresponsibly ignoring the family's needs`
    AND (`the respondent`'s `months of repeated irresponsible gambling` AT LEAST 3 OR `the respondent`'s `particularly irresponsible over a shorter period`)

GIVEN `the respondent` IS A Respondent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a family exclusion order may be made` IF
        `serious harm has been caused` `the respondent`
    AND `the respondent`'s `likely to continue`
    AND `the respondent`'s `given the chance to object`
    AND `the respondent`'s `in the best interests of all`
